# ==============================================================
# .gitignore — Root-level ignore rules for DevSecOps project
# Member 1: Secret Detection Gate
# ==============================================================
#
# DESIGN DECISION for test-secrets/:
# -----------------------------------
# We DO NOT ignore the entire test-secrets/ directory because
# bad.env is intentionally tracked in Git so that Gitleaks can
# scan the committed history and detect the fake secrets during
# the demo.
#
# We DO ignore patterns that could catch accidental REAL secrets,
# such as:
#   *.local.env, *.secret, *.key, .env (root-level)
#
# This means:
#   test-secrets/bad.env   → TRACKED (demo only, fake values)
#   test-secrets/clean.env → TRACKED (safe, no secrets)
#   .env                   → IGNORED (could contain real secrets)
#   *.local.env            → IGNORED (developer overrides)
#   *.secret               → IGNORED (secret files)
# ==============================================================

# ----- Gitleaks binary / tool installation directory -----
# Downloaded with: Invoke-WebRequest + Expand-Archive
# Not source code — should not be committed
gitleaks_install/

# ----- Common real-secret file patterns to ignore -----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example      # Allow example templates

*.secret
*.secrets
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.local.env

# Gitleaks report output (generated files, not source)
gitleaks-report.json
gitleaks-report.sarif
leaks.json

# Member 2: Trivy container scan reports & cache
trivy-report.json
trivy-report.sarif
trivy-results.sarif
.trivy/
.trivy-cache/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
